# The ledger of `chunks`: what Python's LangChain text splitters
# (langchain-text-splitters 1.1.3) and LlamaIndex's node parsers
# (llama-index-core 0.14.26) let a program do with a text cut into pieces for
# retrieval, one block per capability, and what Rebel answers. Neither Go's
# nor Rust's standard library cuts text for retrieval, so their lines read
# `-`; the task named these two as the yardsticks.
#
# The lists are this machine's, 2026-11-18: `dir()` of
# `langchain_text_splitters`, of its `TextSplitter`,
# `RecursiveCharacterTextSplitter` and `MarkdownHeaderTextSplitter` and the
# members of `Language`; `dir()` of `llama_index.core.node_parser` and the
# fields and methods of `SentenceSplitter`, `TokenTextSplitter` and
# `MarkdownNodeParser`; each installed into the scratch folder.
#
# The differential, 2026-11-18, 5,000 generated texts of words of seven
# scripts, emoji and punctuation between runs of spaces, tabs and blank
# lines, sizes 1 to 400 and overlaps 0 to the size less 1: against
# `RecursiveCharacterTextSplitter` with its default separators, 3,007 cases:
# 2,798 made the same pieces as `split_separators` with
# `["\n\n", "\n", " "]` (169 of them once LangChain's pieces of white space
# alone are left out, which it emits untrimmed at its last level), all 1,796
# of a run whose words hold no grapheme of several code points among them,
# and each of the 209 others stood in a text holding one, `e` and U+0301,
# which LangChain cuts apart; against `TokenTextSplitter` in `cl100k_base`, every one of the
# 1,058 texts whose windows end where graphemes end made the same pieces as
# `split_tokens`, and each of the 935 others had LangChain cut inside a
# character and write U+FFFD where `split_tokens` keeps it whole. Cost on
# this Mac at -O2: a megabyte with no space cut to 100 characters in 0.22 s,
# a megabyte of prose to 200 tokens of `cl100k_base` in 0.17 s, a document of
# 10,000 headings in 0.24 s, 102 MB at most.

capability chunk/piece  a piece of a text with where it stands
  heroes  chunks.Chunk
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  langchain_text_splitters.TextSplitter (add_start_index), llama_index.core.node_parser.SentenceSplitter (start_char_idx, end_char_idx of its nodes)
  note    a slice of the text with its byte indices, as a `str` is indexed; LangChain finds a piece's start by searching the text again and LlamaIndex counts characters. A piece of a Markdown document carries its headings' path

capability chunk/measure-characters  sizes counted in characters
  heroes  chunks.by_characters
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  langchain_text_splitters.TextSplitter (length_function=len, chunk_size, chunk_overlap)
  note    code points, as Python's `len`, LangChain's default

capability chunk/measure-bytes  sizes counted in bytes
  heroes  chunks.by_bytes
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  -
  note    the bytes of UTF-8, for a store that limits a field's bytes

capability chunk/measure-tokens  sizes counted in the tokens of a model's encoding
  heroes  chunks.by_tokens
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  langchain_text_splitters.TextSplitter.from_tiktoken_encoder, langchain_text_splitters.TextSplitter.from_huggingface_tokenizer, llama_index.core.node_parser.SentenceSplitter (tokenizer)
  note    `tokenizer`'s encodings; a piece is held to its own count, `tokenizer.count` of its text, its last parts given to the next piece where a join of parts encodes to more than their sum

capability chunk/size  a text measured as the pieces are
  heroes  chunks.size_of
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  -
  note    -

capability chunk/overlap  each piece beginning with the end of the one before
  heroes  chunks.Options
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  langchain_text_splitters.TextSplitter (chunk_overlap), llama_index.core.node_parser.SentenceSplitter (chunk_overlap)
  note    the last whole parts of the piece before that fit in the overlap and leave room for the part after them, as LangChain keeps them; an overlap not below the size is `invalid`, where LangChain raises ValueError

capability chunk/trim  white space at a piece's ends left out
  heroes  chunks.Options
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  langchain_text_splitters.TextSplitter (strip_whitespace)
  note    `trims`, true from `by_characters`, `by_bytes` and `by_tokens` as LangChain's default; a piece of white space alone is then no piece

capability chunk/recursive  a text cut at its coarsest boundaries first and finer only where a part is too large
  heroes  chunks.split
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  langchain_text_splitters.RecursiveCharacterTextSplitter, langchain_text_splitters.TextSplitter.split_text, llama_index.core.node_parser.SentenceSplitter, llama_index.core.node_parser.SentenceSplitter.split_text, llama_index.core.node_parser.SentenceSplitter.split_texts, llama_index.core.node_parser.TextSplitter
  note    paragraphs, then the sentences of UAX #29, then words at white space, then graphemes, never a character cut; LlamaIndex cuts sentences with NLTK's punkt, a model of English, and LangChain at lines and spaces. Parts that fit are joined, and a part too large ends the pieces before it, as LangChain's recursive splitter does

capability chunk/separators  a text cut at the separators a program gives, coarsest first
  heroes  chunks.split_separators
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  langchain_text_splitters.RecursiveCharacterTextSplitter (separators, keep_separator), langchain_text_splitters.CharacterTextSplitter, llama_index.core.node_parser.TokenTextSplitter (separator, backup_separators)
  note    each separator begins the part after it, LangChain's default for its recursive splitter (`keep_separator=True`); graphemes after the last, where LangChain's "" cuts code points. A separator inside a grapheme is passed over

capability chunk/separator-patterns  separators given as regular expressions
  heroes  pending
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  langchain_text_splitters.RecursiveCharacterTextSplitter (is_separator_regex), llama_index.core.node_parser.SentenceSplitter (secondary_chunking_regex)
  note    `regex` would find them; not written this round

capability chunk/levels  a text cut only at one kind of boundary, and the boundaries themselves
  heroes  chunks.split_at, chunks.boundaries, chunks.Level
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  langchain_text_splitters.CharacterTextSplitter (separator), llama_index.core.node_parser.SentenceSplitter (paragraph_separator, chunking_tokenizer_fn)
  note    paragraphs, lines, sentences, words, graphemes; a part larger than the size is a piece alone, as LangChain's CharacterTextSplitter leaves it with a warning

capability chunk/tokens  a text cut into runs of its own tokens
  heroes  chunks.split_tokens
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  langchain_text_splitters.TokenTextSplitter, langchain_text_splitters.split_text_on_tokens, langchain_text_splitters.Tokenizer, llama_index.core.node_parser.TokenTextSplitter
  note    cut only where a token ends at a grapheme's end, where LangChain cuts any token boundary and decodes a character cut in two as U+FFFD; the differential above. Not trimmed, as LangChain's pieces are not

capability chunk/markdown  a Markdown document cut at its headings, each piece with the headings above it
  heroes  chunks.split_markdown
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  langchain_text_splitters.MarkdownHeaderTextSplitter, langchain_text_splitters.MarkdownHeaderTextSplitter.split_text, langchain_text_splitters.MarkdownHeaderTextSplitter.aggregate_lines_to_chunks, langchain_text_splitters.ExperimentalMarkdownSyntaxTextSplitter, langchain_text_splitters.MarkdownTextSplitter, langchain_text_splitters.HeaderType, langchain_text_splitters.LineType, llama_index.core.node_parser.MarkdownNodeParser, llama_index.core.node_parser.MarkdownElementNodeParser
  note    `markdown.parse` says which headings stand at the document's top; each is found among the lines, outside fenced code, and held to the tree's level and text, or the call fails `unsupported`, since `markdown` gives no node a position (its ledger's md/source-positions). Pieces are slices of the source with their heading lines, as LlamaIndex keeps them; LangChain rewrites the lines and strips the headings by default. A section too large is cut by `split`

capability chunk/markdown-levels  only some levels of headings cutting a document
  heroes  pending
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  langchain_text_splitters.MarkdownHeaderTextSplitter (headers_to_split_on, custom_header_patterns, return_each_line, strip_headers)
  note    every level cuts here; the levels a caller names, and a heading's line left out of its piece, wait

capability chunk/hierarchy  pieces of several sizes, each within a larger one
  heroes  chunks.split
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  llama_index.core.node_parser.HierarchicalNodeParser, llama_index.core.node_parser.get_leaf_nodes, llama_index.core.node_parser.get_root_nodes, llama_index.core.node_parser.get_child_nodes, llama_index.core.node_parser.get_deeper_nodes
  note    `split` at each size; a smaller piece lies in the larger whose `start` and `end` hold its own

capability chunk/sentence-window  each sentence with the sentences around it
  heroes  chunks.boundaries
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  llama_index.core.node_parser.SentenceWindowNodeParser
  note    the sentences' boundaries; a window is the slice from one some sentences before to one some after

capability chunk/code  code cut at the separators of its language, or by its syntax tree
  heroes  refused: the separators of a language are a list the program gives `split_separators`; LangChain's lists for 27 languages are its own choices, and LlamaIndex's code splitter parses with tree-sitter, a grammar of each language, which Rebel holds for none
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  langchain_text_splitters.RecursiveCharacterTextSplitter.from_language, langchain_text_splitters.RecursiveCharacterTextSplitter.get_separators_for_language, langchain_text_splitters.Language, langchain_text_splitters.PythonCodeTextSplitter, langchain_text_splitters.LatexTextSplitter, langchain_text_splitters.JSFrameworkTextSplitter, llama_index.core.node_parser.CodeSplitter, llama_index.core.node_parser.LanguageConfig
  note    -

